cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QuDock or QuDock-Bench, please cite it as below."
title: "QuDock: quantum kernels vs classical models for BACE-1 inhibitor screening"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shubhodeep
    family-names: Chatterjee
  - given-names: Srijita
    family-names: Banerjee
  - given-names: Rounak
    family-names: Pal
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/vtu-qiskit-fall-fest-2026/vtu-hc-blackout"
url: "https://qudock-blackout.streamlit.app/"
keywords:
  - quantum machine learning
  - quantum kernels
  - drug discovery
  - Alzheimer's disease
  - BACE-1
  - virtual screening
abstract: >-
  QuDock tests whether quantum kernels help find BACE-1 inhibitors, a key
  Alzheimer's drug target, when data is scarce and hardware is noisy. It
  compares ZZ, projected, trainable and pharmacophore-graph quantum kernels
  with strong classical baselines on scaffold splits, measures kernels on IBM
  Quantum hardware, and ships QuDock-Bench, a fixed protocol for scoring any
  molecule classifier on BACE, BBBP and ClinTox.
